        "content": "# Module 16: First Job, CTC Breakdown and Corporate Benefits\n\n**(CAMPUS TO CORPORATE FINANCIAL SURVIVAL GUIDE)**\n\nBrother/Sister, congratulations! You cleared the placement drive in your college's final year, the HR smiled in the campus interview and said *\"We are happy to offer you a CTC of Rs.12 lakhs per annum!\"*, and you instantly posted a status on your college WhatsApp group, *\"Offer accepted! Rs.1 lakh per month package!\"* Friends ordered food from Zomato/Swiggy, parents distributed sweets in the whole neighborhood, and you started mentally checking the prices of Nifty 50 Index Fund SIPs, a new scooter EMI, and flagship phones on iOS vs Android.\n\nBut then reality hits. On the 30th date of your first month at the job, when the salary credit SMS arrives in your bank account: *\"Credited INR 81,800\"*, you go into deep shock. You refresh the screen again and again and think: *\"Brother! Rs.12 lakhs divided by 12 months should be exactly Rs.1,00,000 per month! Where did my Rs.18,200 per month go? Did HR cheat me? Did the company deduct fraudulent amounts? Or did the government take all my money as income tax?\"*\n\nWelcome to the real corporate world!\n\nThe corporate salary structure is like a multi-dimensional jigsaw puzzle where HR managers and compensation teams arrange components in such a way that the CTC offer letter looks maximum and shiny, but the actual bank balance gets credited with modest real values. In this module, we will decode everything from the single line CTC on your placement offer letter to PF arrears, ESOP vesting schedules, tax deductions, corporate perks, flexi benefit baskets, and layoff severance packages — **all with surgical precision**.",
