        "title": "CTC vs In-Hand Salary — Reality Check (Part 3)",
        "content": "### 16.1.5 CTC Red Flags in Placement Offer Letters\n\nBefore clicking \"Accept Offer\" on your placement portal, audit your offer letter for these 7 dangerous CTC traps:\n\n#### 1. The Laptop / Infrastructure Rental Depreciation Charge\nSome aggressive early-stage companies include laptop lease costs, desk rental space, or cloud server credits into the employee's CTC package!\n*Rule:* Equipment provided for work is a business expense, NOT employee compensation.\n\n#### 2. Excessive Variable Pay Component (> 25% of CTC)\nIf more than 25-30% of your CTC is variable pay tied to \"individual and company performance\", your actual take-home will fluctuate wildly. In bad quarters, you may receive 0% variable pay.\n\n#### 3. Multi-Year Stock Grants Dressed as Year-1 CTC\nAs shown above, 4-year RSU grants should NOT be counted as Year-1 income. Calculate your Year-1 real cash: Fixed + Bonus + Joining + Year-1 Vested Stock only.\n\n#### 4. Signing Bonus With Clawback Clause\nMany companies offer Rs.1-2 lakh signing bonus but include a clause: \"If you leave within 12 months, the full bonus must be returned.\" This is essentially an interest-free loan, not a bonus.\n\n#### 5. Gratuity Included in CTC from Day 1\nGratuity is payable only after 5 years of continuous service. Including it in Year-1 CTC is misleading — most freshers leave within 2-3 years and forfeit the entire gratuity pool.\n\n#### 6. Insurance Premium Shown as Cash Benefit\nGroup health insurance premium paid by the company is a non-cash benefit. Showing Rs.12,000-15,000 insurance premium as part of CTC inflates the headline number.\n\n#### 7. Training Bond / Service Agreement Penalty\nSome companies include a 1-2 year training bond with a penalty of Rs.2-5 lakhs if you leave early. This is NOT a benefit — it is a liability that restricts your career mobility.\n\n---",
