        "title": "Corporate Perks and Flexi-Benefits Optimization (Part 3)",
        "content": "### 16.4.4 Medical Insurance — Cashless vs Reimbursement: When to Use What\n\n| Scenario | Cashless Claim | Reimbursement Claim |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Preferred Hospital in Network** | YES — Hospital bills insurance directly | Not needed |\n| **Preferred Hospital NOT in Network** | Not available | Submit bills within 15-30 days |\n| **Emergency Hospitalization (any hospital)** | Request cashless from any network hospital | If cashless denied, pay and claim reimbursement |\n| **Planned Surgery** | Always use cashless at network hospital | Avoid reimbursement — delayed payment |\n| **Day Care Procedures** | Check if procedure is covered under cashless | Submit for reimbursement if not covered |\n\n> **Pro Tip:** Always carry your corporate health insurance card. Know your policy number and TPAT (Third Party Administrator) helpline number. In emergencies, call the TPA helpline first to activate cashless approval.",
