        "title": "Glossary of 20 Corporate Financial Terms",
        "content": "1. **CTC (Cost to Company):** Total annual expense an employer incurs on an employee.\n2. **Gross Salary:** Total direct cash earnings before statutory deductions (PF, PT, TDS).\n3. **Net / Take-Home Salary:** Final cash amount credited to the employee's bank account.\n4. **Basic Salary:** Core foundational component of salary (usually 40-50% of CTC).\n5. **HRA (House Rent Allowance):** Allowance provided to cover rental housing costs.\n6. **EPF (Employees' Provident Fund):** Statutory retirement savings scheme managed by EPFO.\n7. **EPS (Employees' Pension Scheme):** Pension fund portion (8.33% capped at Rs.1,250/mo) of employer PF.\n8. **VPF (Voluntary Provident Fund):** Additional voluntary employee contribution to EPF pool.\n9. **Gratuity:** Statutory lump-sum benefit paid after completing 5 years of continuous service.\n10. **ESOP (Employee Stock Option Plan):** Right to purchase company shares at a pre-set strike price.\n11. **RSU (Restricted Stock Unit):** Direct grant of company shares issued upon meeting vesting criteria.\n12. **Grant Date:** Official date when stock options or RSUs are awarded to an employee.\n13. **Vesting Schedule:** Timeline over which stock grants become exercisable by the employee.\n14. **Cliff Period:** Minimum waiting period (typically 1 year) before initial stock vesting occurs.\n15. **Strike Price / Exercise Price:** Fixed price per share an employee pays to exercise ESOP options.\n16. **Perquisite Tax:** Income tax charged at slab rate on non-cash benefits or stock option gains.\n17. **Corporate NPS (80CCD(2)):** Employer pension contribution deductible up to 10% of Basic pay.\n18. **Flexi Benefit Basket (FBB):** Tax-exempt reimbursable allowance options offered by employers.\n19. **UAN (Universal Account Number):** Permanent 12-digit number linking all EPF accounts of an individual.\n20. **Form 16:** Statutory certificate issued by employers detailing salary paid and TDS withheld.\n\n---",
